Package: convertible-power
Architecture: all
Depends: tlp (>= 1.6), upower, python3, python3-gi, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: thermald, powertop, gir1.2-glib-2.0
Conflicts: power-profiles-daemon
Description: power settings: performance on AC, efficiency on battery
 Shared power settings for the device packages in this family: TLP settings
 (maximum performance on AC power, maximum battery life on battery), UPower
 settings that hibernate at 10% charge, and a small user service that reminds
 you to unplug at 80% on machines whose firmware cannot stop charging itself.
 .
 Device packages add their own TLP drop-in after this one, for the parts that
 depend on the hardware (CPU frequency driver, USB devices that must never be
 suspended, platform profiles).
 .
 TLP replaces power-profiles-daemon (the two cannot run together), so the
 GNOME "Power Mode" switch goes away; AC and battery are handled automatically.
